Fix: Proxy Socket.io through Vite for ngrok compatibility

Problem: Client couldn't connect to server via ngrok because
socket was hardcoded to localhost:3001

Solution:
- Added Vite proxy for /socket.io -> localhost:3001
- Changed socket URL to window.location.origin (same as page)
- Now only ONE ngrok tunnel needed (port 5173)

How it works:
- ngrok URL -> Vite dev server (5173)
- Vite proxies /socket.io -> backend (3001)
- Everything works through single ngrok tunnel!

